=== Summary: both evidence references are retained on the token in
=== submission order, with SubmittedByMsp correctly showing the Fabric-
=== authenticated caller identity (Org1MSP) rather than the caller-supplied
=== ProducerMsp field (Tier1SupplierMSP) -- the same distinction the
=== dissertation's discussion of this extension makes in prose, now backed
=== by a real transaction rather than only a unit test. Both negative cases
=== (duplicate evidence ID, malformed digest) were rejected as designed,
=== with no partial write: a repeat GetEvidence query (not shown above,
=== run manually) confirmed the token's evidence array still contained
=== exactly the two accepted references, not three.
